# `sum = sum + blend(low, high, share)` in a loop, in a file without types. `blend` is `a + b * c` and has no loop of its own; `low`, `high` and `share` are constants of the file whose values come out of
# a text at run time. The copy of `blend` stands in the caller's loop, so its product is a product in a loop; what it reckons with stays the same through the turns, so each is asked once, in front of the
# loop, whether it is a number. Behind "yes" the turns add one number. `blend` by itself, outside any loop, asks nothing.
# f1 = blend, f2 = total, f3 = other
